title: 'feat(webrtc): derive DTLS certificate deterministically from node key'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    # Description

    Derives the WebRTC DTLS certificate deterministically from the node's Ed25519 secret key instead of persisting it to a separate file on disk.

    # Integration
    Previously, the DTLS certificate was either persisted to a `webrtc_certificate` file in the network config dir, or generated when no config dir was set, causing the certhash to change on every restart for such nodes. #12621 updated it to be managed exactly as a node secrete key.

    While this PR change the approach entirely and instead uses the node secret key as a seed for a deterministically generated WebRTC certificate.

    A new optional `--webrtc-seed <u64>` flag rotates that certificate: the seed is appended to the key-derivation domain-separation tag, so the certhash changes while the node key and peer id stay the same. Without the flag the derivation is unchanged.

    ## Review Notes

    `derive_certificate` derives a P-256 signing key from the 32-byte node key seed via RFC 9380 `hash_to_field` then builds a minimal self-signed X.509 certificate and loads it into litep2p's `DtlsCertificate`.

    #### Note

    WebRTC certificate derivation needs `sha2` 0.11 to match the `digest` 0.11 traits used by `p256` 0.14 and `hash2curve` 0.14. I didn't bump the main version because it was not straightforward, precisely, `sp-core` has `w3f-bls` as a dependency, which is not compatible with `sha2` 0.11. Do you have any suggestions to handle this? Should this version pinning be kept?
crates:
- name: sc-cli
  bump: major
- name: sc-network
  bump: major
